2. **Closed tickets and rating.** Requirement 1 says "a resolved ticket"; the acceptance criteria only test open/
   pending refusal. Recommend resolved-only — closed is refused with the same error as open/pending. Proceeding on
   that basis.
3. **Where the weekly summary lives.** No external reader is named for it (unlike the finance export). Recommend a
   queryable store record (`getAgentSummary`/`setAgentSummary`) the back office reads live, not a snapshot file.
   Proceeding on that basis.
4. **Editing a rating afterwards.** Not in the spec. Recommend no edit/delete — "the first one stays as it was"
   reads as permanent. Proceeding without an edit path.

Assumption, not asked (defaults if it turns out wrong): a low score on a ticket with no owner (never assigned) is
stored without a notification — there is no one to email.

